# Git Workflow Commands (Voice Triggers)

When the user says one of these phrases, follow the matching playbook. Do **not** ask which files to stage unless the command is ambiguous or secrets are present.

| User says | Action |
|---|---|
| **`git commit all`** | Full playbook below: discover scopes → branch per scope → commit each → **push all** new/updated task branches → return to `main` → brief report |
| **`git commit`** | Same as `git commit all`, but **push only if** the user also said push in the same message; otherwise commit locally and list branches/SHAs |
| **`git workflow`** | Read-only audit + optional commit (see Workflow Audit) |

---

## Scoped implementation = one branch

Split work when the diff spans **different purposes** (not every file):

| Signal | Branch prefix | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Bug / regression / auth loop | `fix/` | `fix/auth-session-bridge` |
| New capability | `feat/` | `feat/local-test-account` |
| Refactor only | `refactor/` | `refactor/popup-events-extraction` |
| Rules / docs only | `docs/` | `docs/git-workflow-commands` |

**Reuse** the latest related task branch when the diff is a direct follow-up on the same topic (e.g. more credit-pack UI on `feat/credit-packs-billing`).

**Never** commit unrelated scopes on one branch. **Never** push to `main` unless the user explicitly approves.

---

## `git commit all` — agent playbook

### 1. Discover

Run in parallel:

- `git branch --show-current`
- `git status --short`
- `git diff --stat` (and spot-check hunks if grouping is unclear)
- `git stash list`
- `git branch -a` (recent `fix/*`, `feat/*` on origin)

### 2. Group files by scope

Use path + diff intent. PasteCraft common scopes:

| Scope | Typical paths |
|---|---|
| Credit packs / AI Lab billing | `extension/popup/features/ai-lab/ai-lab.credit-packs.js`, `ai-lab.credits.js`, `tests/credit-pack-banner.test.mjs` |
| Local test account | `extension/popup/features/auth/local-test-account.js`, `auth.constants.js`, `auth.events.js`, `popup.init.js`, `popup.html` (test banner/button), `styles.css`, `sync.listener.js`, `full-sync.js` |
| Auth session / bridge | `extension/popup/features/auth/auth.service.js`, `extension/supabase/auth.js`, `identity.js` |
| Website / Netlify | `website/**`, `netlify.toml` |
| Supabase migrations / Edge | `supabase/migrations/**`, `supabase/functions/**` |

If one file mixes scopes (rare), split hunks across branches or commit with the dominant scope and note the rest in the report.

### 3. Stash if multiple scopes on one checkout

```powershell
git stash push -u -m "multi-scope-wip-<yyyy-mm-dd>"
```

### 4. Commit each scope (order: fix → feat → docs)

For **each** scope:

1. `git checkout main` && `git pull origin main`
2. Reuse `git checkout <existing-branch>` **or** `git checkout -b <prefix>/<topic>`
3. Restore only that scope’s files:
   - Tracked: `git checkout "stash@{0}" -- <paths>`
   - Stash untracked: `git checkout "stash@{0}^3" -- <paths>`
4. Commit with a short title + optional body (minimal text per user preference)
5. `git push -u origin HEAD`

After all scopes: `git checkout main`, `git stash drop` if fully applied.

### 5. Report (required)

```
git commit all — done
- fix/auth-session-bridge @ <sha> — auth bridge token freshness
- feat/local-test-account @ <sha> — offline demo account
- feat/credit-packs-billing @ <sha> — credit pack banner + tests
Branch: main (clean)
```

Say out loud before the first commit:

> Phase: commit all. Scopes: N. Branches: [list]. Action: stash → split → push.

---

## `git workflow` — audit + reconcile

Use when the user wants a **repo-wide** picture, including work from **other finished chats** that may not be in the current thread.

### 1. Local repo

- `git status --short`, `git diff --stat`, `git stash list`
- Branches ahead of `origin/main`: `git branch -vv`, `git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline` per local branch

### 2. Cross-chat context (read-only)

Scan **recent** parent transcripts under the project’s `agent-transcripts/` folder (not subagents):

- Search for: `SUCCESS`, `feat/`, `fix/`, uncommitted paths, “stash”, “branch”
- Correlate with local `git status` / stashes / unpushed branches

Do not invent work that is not in git or transcripts.

### 3. Program logs (if present)

- `program-study/success/SuccessLog.md`, `partial/PartialLog.md`, `failure/FailureLog.md`
- `implementations.md` / `bugfixes.md` for pending items

### 4. Output format

```markdown
## Git workflow — <date>

### Uncommitted (this checkout)
- [scope]: files…

### Stashes
- stash@{n}: …

### Unpushed / open task branches
- branch @ ahead N — topic — action (push / PR / merge / abandon)

### From other chats (if found)
- [title](uuid) — topic — likely branch or files

### Recommended next command
- `git commit all` — if scopes are ready and verified
- or: verify with user before commit
```

If the user says **`git workflow` then commit**, run the audit first, then `git commit all` unless they only wanted the report.

